{"date": "2026-09-21", "title": "Pop Culture Digest — Monday, September 21, 2026", "link": "https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/", "pubDate": "Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0500", "description": "\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n\n  <tr><td style=\"background:#111111;padding:24px 18px 20px;color:#ffffff;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c9a66b;\">Monday · September 21, 2026</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin-top:8px;font-weight:normal;\">Pop Culture Digest</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#d0d0d0;margin-top:8px;\">What’s actually dominating today</div>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:18px 18px 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#444;\">\n    Four stories owning the conversation this morning: the Gerber family mourns Presley at 27, <em>Monster</em>’s Lizzie Borden season locks Netflix’s No. 1 despite soft reviews, BTS closes iHeartFest with an ARIRANG-era set, and Zach Cregger’s <em>Resident Evil</em> gets Monday confirmation as a franchise-record opener.\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 1 Presley Gerber -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be185d;font-weight:600;\">Celebrity</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Presley Gerber, son of Cindy Crawford and Rande Gerber, dies at 27</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/us/cindy-crawfords-son-presley-gerber-dies-aged-27-2026-09-21/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/img1.jpg\" alt=\"Presley Gerber\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Presley Walker Gerber — model, brother of Kaia, and the only son of Cindy Crawford and Rande Gerber — died Sunday, Sept. 20, at a Los Angeles rehabilitation facility, according to Los Angeles County Medical Examiner records. He was 27. A family representative asked for privacy “during this very difficult and painful time”; an autopsy is pending and no cause of death has been released.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/us/cindy-crawfords-son-presley-gerber-dies-aged-27-2026-09-21/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_reuters.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Reuters&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2026/09/21/presley-gerber-dead/91868902007/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_usatoday.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">USA Today&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://abcnews.com/US/cindy-crawfords-son-presley-gerber-dies-27/story?id=136609656\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_abc.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">ABC News&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 2 Monster -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;font-weight:600;\">Streaming</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\"><em>Monster: The Lizzie Borden Story</em> is Netflix’s No. 1 — at 44% RT</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.comingsoon.net/tv/news/2194232-monster-season-4-lizzie-borden-story-netflix-no-1\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/img2.jpg\" alt=\"Monster The Lizzie Borden Story\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Season 4 of Ryan Murphy and Ian Brennan’s anthology dropped all eight episodes Sept. 17 and has held Netflix’s U.S. TV No. 1 for three straight days (FlixPatrol). Ella Beatty leads as Lizzie, with Charlie Hunnam, Rebecca Hall, Vicky Krieps, and Sarah Paulson in the ensemble — while critics sit at roughly 44% on Rotten Tomatoes. Audiences clearly didn’t wait for the reviews.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.comingsoon.net/tv/news/2194232-monster-season-4-lizzie-borden-story-netflix-no-1\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_comingsoon.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">ComingSoon&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/tv/reviews/monster-the-lizzie-borden-story-review-netflix-1236858761/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety review&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.netflix.com/title/82068293\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_netflix.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Netflix&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 3 BTS -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7c3aed;font-weight:600;\">Live Music</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">BTS closes iHeartFest night one with an ARIRANG-era mic drop</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.iheart.com/content/2026-09-19-bts-fiery-set-at-the-2026-iheartradio-music-festival-was-the-ultimate-mic-drop/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/img3.jpg\" alt=\"BTS at iHeartRadio Music Festival\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">At T-Mobile Arena in Las Vegas on Friday, Sept. 18, BTS closed night one of the 2026 iHeartRadio Music Festival — their first in-person iHeartFest appearance. The set opened with ARIRANG lead single “SWIM,” rolled into “2.0,” hit classic “MIC Drop,” and finished with “FYA” under onstage flames. The full septet’s post-hiatus era is very much a live product now.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.iheart.com/content/2026-09-19-bts-fiery-set-at-the-2026-iheartradio-music-festival-was-the-ultimate-mic-drop/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_iheart.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">iHeart&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 4 Resident Evil Monday -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:22px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9a3412;font-weight:600;\">Movies</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\"><em>Resident Evil</em> locks a franchise-record $60M — Monday confirmation</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://abcnews.com/Entertainment/wireStory/box-office-resident-evil-tops-box-office-franchise-136601474\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/img4.jpg\" alt=\"Resident Evil 2026\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\">\n    </a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">AP and Variety Monday wrap: Zach Cregger’s reboot opened to about $60M domestic and $108.3M worldwide — both franchise highs — from 3,684 locations on a ~$75M budget. Still the weekend’s loudest theatrical story as Monday numbers harden.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://abcnews.com/Entertainment/wireStory/box-office-resident-evil-tops-box-office-franchise-136601474\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_abc.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">AP via ABC&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/resident-evil-box-office-zach-cregger-reboot-opening-weekend-record-breaking-1236867659/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XKOVrTqXncw\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-21/images/fav_youtube.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Trailer&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- Bottom of the news -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#111;font-weight:700;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-top:22px;\">Bottom of the news</div>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:8px 18px 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#333;\">\n    <ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18px;\">\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Ed Sheeran’s Philly LOOP stop (Lincoln Financial Field, Sat.): he nearly scrapped the tour after Macklemore fallout; called it “the best show of my life.”</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Lucas Museum of Narrative Art opens to the public Tuesday in L.A. after Saturday’s star-studded gala.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><em>Spider-Man: Brand New Day</em> still ~$944.5M domestic / ~$2.45B WW (all-time domestic No. 1).</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><em>Practical Magic 2</em> slid ~60% to ~$12M in weekend two (~$49M domestic to date).</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">New Found Glory’s Chad Gilbert mourned at 45; Jhené Aiko’s <em>Westside Whimsy</em> still sits atop the Billboard 200.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Tom Morello’s Power To The People (Oct. 3, Merriweather) adds Geezer Butler, Scott Ian, Mike McCready, and more.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Madonna × Charli XCX “Danceteria Afterhours” still due Sept. 24; Madonna into the VMAs with 11 noms.</li>\n      <li style=\"margin:0;\">Next weekend: Brad Pitt’s <em>Heart of the Beast</em>, DreamWorks’ <em>Forgotten Island</em>, A24’s <em>Primetime</em> (Robert Pattinson).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 36px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#888;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    Pop Culture Digest · Monday, September 21, 2026<br>\n    Full-bleed mobile layout · from popculture@agentmail.to\n  </td></tr>\n\n</table>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n"}